## 2. Origin & Redirect Guards

### A. Origin Evaluation in `src/proxy.ts`
- **Origin check location:** [src/proxy.ts#L15-L35](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/proxy.ts#L15-L35) calling [src/lib/security/origin.ts#L155-L205](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/lib/security/origin.ts#L155-L205).
- **Behavior:**
  - Evaluates `Origin` on state-changing methods (`POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`).
  - Same-origin requests pass if `request.headers.get('origin') === request.nextUrl.origin` ([origin.ts#L181-L191](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/lib/security/origin.ts#L181-L191)).
  - Cross-origin requests are checked against `getTrustedOrigins()` ([origin.ts#L74-L142](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/lib/security/origin.ts#L74-L142)): `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL`, `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`, and `VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL`.
  - **Risk:** If the application is accessed via an unlisted custom domain or Vercel preview domain where `origin` doesn't match `nextUrl.origin`, `POST /api/auth/login` and `POST /api/auth/register` will be blocked with **HTTP 403 `Cross-origin request blocked.`**.

### B. Environment App URL (`getAppUrl()`)
- **Location:** [src/services/auth.service.ts#L29-L55](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/services/auth.service.ts#L29-L55)
- **Behavior:**
  ```ts
  const isProduction =
    process.env.VERCEL_ENV === 'production' ||
    (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' && !process.env.VERCEL_ENV);

  if (isProduction) {
    throw new AppError(
      'NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL must be configured in production environment',
      500,
      'APP_URL_NOT_CONFIGURED'
    );
  }
  ```
- **Risk:** In production, if `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` is missing:
  - `AuthService.register()` crashes with **HTTP 500**.
  - `sendPasswordResetEmail()` and `resendVerificationEmail()` fail to generate callback URLs.
  - If `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` is set to a production domain (e.g. `https://cpilancers.com`) but users test on Vercel (`https://cpilancers-*.vercel.app`), email verification links will point to the custom domain instead of the current deployment.

### C. Protected Route Redirects in `src/proxy.ts`
- **Location:** [src/proxy.ts#L41-L70](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/proxy.ts#L41-L70)
- **Protected regex:** `/^\/(profile|messages|proposals|contracts|dashboard|jobs\/create|jobs\/[^/]+\/(edit|proposals))(\/|$)/`
- **Bug with `/dashboard`:**
  - An unauthenticated user hitting `/dashboard` gets redirected to `/login?next=/dashboard`.
  - Upon successful login, `resolvePostLoginPath` preserves the valid `next` path and sends them to `/dashboard`.
  - **`/dashboard` does not exist as a page**, producing an immediate **HTTP 404**.

