## 4. Rate-Limit UX Analysis

### Where Auth Errors Are Mapped
1. **Registration:** [src/services/auth.service.ts#L145-L151](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/services/auth.service.ts#L145-L151)
   ```ts
   if (authError) {
     if (authError.code === 'user_already_exists') {
       throw new ConflictError('An account with this email already exists.');
     }
     throw new AppError(authError.message, 400, 'AUTH_SIGNUP_ERROR');
   }
   ```
   - When Supabase Auth rate limits signup emails (`over_email_send_rate_limit` or HTTP 429), `authError.message` is `"For security purposes, you can only request this once every 60 seconds"`.
   - It is thrown as an `AUTH_SIGNUP_ERROR` (HTTP 400), and displayed directly in [src/app/(auth)/register/page.tsx#L107-L111](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/app/(auth)/register/page.tsx#L107-L111).
2. **Login:** [src/services/auth.service.ts#L221-L224](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/services/auth.service.ts#L221-L224)
   - Catches all Supabase errors and masks them with `throw new UnauthorizedError('Invalid email or password.')`.
   - If Supabase rate limits IP/email attempts (`over_request_rate_limit`), the user is given no indication of lockout/rate limiting.
3. **Password Reset & Resend Verification:** [src/services/auth.service.ts#L277-L283](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/services/auth.service.ts#L277-L283) & [src/services/auth.service.ts#L391-L397](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/services/auth.service.ts#L391-L397)
   - To prevent account enumeration, both methods swallow errors and return `{ success: true }`.
   - However, when rate-limited (`over_email_send_rate_limit`), the UI tells the user an email was dispatched even though Supabase rejected it.
4. **Missing Error Hierarchy in `src/lib/errors.ts`:**
   - There is no `RateLimitError` or HTTP 429 status code handling in [src/lib/errors.ts](file:///c:/projects/cpilancers/src/lib/errors.ts).

